) suggests reasonable measurement validity", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability", "measurement validity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "Selection bias item label"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "the 14.7% of dyads excluded for missing photos were not missing at random", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missingness", "selection bias"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[164, 164]], "note": "players without photos may systematically differ (e.g., less prominent players)"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "restates the earlier fact that 7.3% were excluded for missing covariates"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "Ecological fallacy item label"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "referee country-level IAT aggregated from online samples may not represent actual referees"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "did not have individual-level referee implicit bias measures, only country-level aggregates", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee implicit bias measurement"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[171, 171]], "note": "Confounding subheading"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "controlled confounders were games played, position, league, height, weight, and referee country bias", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["controlled confounders"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "Potential uncontrolled confounders lead-in"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 180]], "assertion": "did not control for player behavior/aggression, player reputation/history with the referee, match context, playing-style differences correlated with skin tone, or team-level tactical factors", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["uncontrolled confounders"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "Statistical Considerations subheading"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "made no formal adjustment for multiple comparisons, justified by there being only one primary hypothesis", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple comparisons adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "very wide confidence interval indicates substantial uncertainty"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "p=0.048 just below α=0.05; result could be sensitive to model specification"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "Clustered data structure item label"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "each player appears in ~81 dyads on average", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dyads per player"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "clustering may not fully capture the complex dependence structure"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "referee-level clustering was not modeled, though implicitly controlled via position/league", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[195, 195]], "note": "Causal Interpretation subheading"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[197, 197]], "assertion": "despite controlling for measured confounders, the observational design means causation cannot be definitively established", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["causal inference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[198, 200]], "note": "lists possible alternative explanations for the association: direct bias, omitted confounders, residual confounding"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[201, 201]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[202, 202]], "note": "Generalizability subheading"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "sample restricted to four European leagues in one season"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "lead-in to generalizability caveats list"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[206, 209]], "note": "results may not generalize to other regions, time periods, sports, or women's soccer"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[210, 210]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "Conclusion heading"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[215, 215]], "assertion": "the hypothesis that referees are more likely to give red cards to dark-skinned players is statistically supported, with adjusted risk difference 0.19pp (95% CI [0.001,0.382], p=0.048)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 216]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[217, 217]], "assertion": "the effect size is small: an absolute increase of less than 0.2pp on a baseline of ~1.2%, a modest practical difference", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[219, 219]], "assertion": "statistical significance is marginal: p=0.048 barely crosses the conventional threshold and the CI lower bound is 0.001", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value", "confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[220, 220]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[221, 221]], "assertion": "there is substantial uncertainty: the 95% CI is wide, ranging from essentially zero to 0.38pp", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[222, 222]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[223, 223]], "assertion": "the effect becomes non-significant with a more stringent dark-skin cutoff (≥0.625), possibly reflecting reduced statistical power", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity to specification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[225, 225]], "assertion": "despite controlling for key confounders, the observational design precludes definitive causal inference", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["causal inference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[226, 226]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[227, 227]], "assertion": "the effect, though small, is in the hypothesized direction and persists after extensive covariate adjustment including referee country implicit bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[228, 228]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 229]], "assertion": "a 0.19pp increase translates to roughly 1 additional red card per 500 encounters, or about 0.15 additional red cards over an ~80-encounter career", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["practical significance"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[231, 235]], "note": "research implications and suggested directions for future research, not claims about this analysis"}]}}